This is a remote position.
On behalf of our Client - a global consulting company which is building its SAP implementation team in Poland - we are looking for an experienced Principal SAP QM Consultant, who will work on global implementation and transformation projects.
In the role, you will:

• Manage full lifecycle implementations of SAP S/4HANA in the area of Quality Management (QM), including integration with Production Planning (PP) and Manufacturing Execution;

• Evaluate business requirements, identify relevant SAP capabilities and apply best practices;

• Plan, prepare and execute Fit-Gap / Fit-to-Standard workshops with business stakeholders;

• Perform solution design and drive adoption for identified gaps and business process improvements;

• Ensure high-quality system implementation in collaboration with delivery teams (including near-/offshore);

• Act as a sparring partner for the client and support key decision-making processes;

• Take on project management responsibilities where required;

• Support international rollout projects across multiple locations.

Our Client is a dynamic, fast-growing consulting organization with a strong ERP & Platforms practice, specializing in delivering innovative and transformational SAP S/4HANA solutions for some of the world’s largest organizations. Recognized in the market for its entrepreneurial culture, high-impact projects, and strong focus on people development, the company offers structured career paths, continuous learning opportunities, and exposure to cutting-edge SAP technologies. Working in an international and multicultural environment, you will have the opportunity to grow your career while contributing to large-scale transformation programs.
Requirements

• Higher education degree in Economics, Information Technology or equivalent;

• Minimum 10 years of SAP consulting experience, with strong focus on SAP QM;

• At least 2-5 full project lifecycles in SAP implementations;

• Proven experience in SAP S/4HANA projects and/or certification;

• Strong knowledge of Quality Management processes (inspection planning, results recording, quality notifications, quality certificates);

• Solid understanding of Production Planning;

• Ability to translate business requirements into system design specifications;

• Experience in international template rollout projects is a strong advantage;

• Strong communication, stakeholder management, and problem-solving skills;

• Fluent English (C2); additional European languages are a plus;

• Self-starter, proactive, and team-oriented mindset;

• Willingness to travel if required.

Benefits

• REMOTE work in European implementation and transformation projects;

• Industry-leading compensation and benefits;

• Working with latest SAP technologies;

• Exposure to strategic projects, where you’ll be able to see your own ideas transform into breakthrough results;

• Being an important part of a diverse and talented consulting team;

• Work in an innovation-driven practice and a high-performance culture;

• Top training and development opportunities;

• True possibility to grow your career and achieve your personal ambitions.

